// spec: `T x;` (a local, a global, an array of T, a static member defined outside its class) of a class without a default constructor is the checker's error naming why, as `new T` is (language/new_of_a_class_without_a_default_constructor_is_error): a deleted one, a reference member or a const scalar member without an initializer, a member of a class without one. Codegen said it "does not support default construction" (kovarex, 2026-11-17); other constructors alone leave the implicit one (classes/implicit_default_constructor_beside_others)
// error: default_initialized_variable_without_default_constructor_is_error.kpp:31: error: Deleted has no default constructor: its default constructor is deleted
// error: default_initialized_variable_without_default_constructor_is_error.kpp:32: error: Holder has no default constructor: its member 'target', a reference, has no initializer
// error: default_initialized_variable_without_default_constructor_is_error.kpp:33: error: Fixed has no default constructor: its const member 'limit' has no initializer
// error: default_initialized_variable_without_default_constructor_is_error.kpp:34: error: Outer has no default constructor: its member 'inner' (Deleted) has none
